Valkey 9.2 release notes
========================

Upgrade urgency levels:

| Level    | Meaning                                                             |
|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| LOW      | No need to upgrade unless there are new features you want to use.   |
| MODERATE | Program an upgrade of the server, but it's not urgent.              |
| HIGH     | There is a critical bug that may affect a subset of users. Upgrade! |
| CRITICAL | There is a critical bug affecting MOST USERS. Upgrade ASAP.         |
| SECURITY | There are security fixes in the release.                            |

Valkey 9.2.0-rc2  -  Released Wed 04 November 2026
--------------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency LOW: This is the second release candidate of Valkey 9.2.0.

### New Features and Enhanced Behavior
* Add new `DELEX` command to conditionally delete a string key when its value matches (`IFEQ`) or differs from (`IFNE`) a given value by @lightsigma96 (#4607)
* Add Zstd as a streaming compression codec for RDB persistence and replication, offering better compression ratios than LZ4 by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#3798)
* Support streaming-compressed RDB preambles in AOF bases, so compressed full-sync RDB files can be reused directly as AOF bases by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4754)
* `ACL GENPASS` and the hash function seed draw randomness from the configured OpenSSL 3 provider when built with TLS, supporting deployments that require a validated crypto module by @MarkAtwood (#4339)
* Support forkless full synchronization to replicas, serving disk and diskless full syncs from a background-thread snapshot without forking by @nitaicaro (#4797)

### Performance and Efficiency Improvements
* Speed up sorted set score updates in listpack encoding by replacing the score in place when the member keeps its position by @charsyam (#3491)
* Fix quadratic slowdown in `HRANDFIELD` and `SRANDMEMBER` with counts on collections whose elements differ only in letter case by @madolson (#5167)
* Bound the time spent per cycle evicting keys from the client tracking table, avoiding long stalls after lowering `tracking-table-max-keys` by @tanmayBeginsJourney (#4775)
* Speed up the `INFO` command by around 5% by pre-allocating the output buffer by @charsyam (#3413)
* Reclaim client-side caching tracking table entries left by disconnected clients, fixing a memory leak under read-heavy workloads, and include the tracking table in active defrag by @rayjinghaolei (#4190)
* Speed up `ZPOPMIN` and `ZPOPMAX` on B+tree encoded sorted sets by detaching edge items without a key search or copy by @charsyam (#4852)
* Counting a hash's fields with expirations is now O(1) for hashtable-encoded hashes by tracking the volatile set size on each mutation by @frostzt (#4829)
* Speed up AOF command propagation by serializing commands directly into the AOF buffer, removing an allocation and copy per command by @charsyam (#3496)
* Cache the earliest event-loop timer to avoid an O(N) scan per iteration, reducing overhead with many timers such as RDMA connections by @royenheart (#4354)
* Speed up HGETALL, HKEYS and HVALS with exact-length reply headers, fused bulk replies, and entry prefetching by @jjuleslasarte (#4417)
* Eliminate false sharing in per-thread memory usage counters, improving throughput with I/O threads on SMT x86 systems by @omerrubi-amzn (#4107)
* Read-only list iteration (e.g. LRANGE, LPOS) no longer decompresses and recompresses quicklist nodes in place, cutting CPU cost on compressed lists by @murphyjacob4 (#4782)
* Speed up ZSCAN on btree-encoded sorted sets by avoiding temporary member and score copies and prefetching items by @charsyam (#4856)
* Reduce cache-line false sharing on IO thread activity and job counters for better multi-threaded IO performance by @omerrubi-amzn (#4976)
* PHDELPREFIX now bounds its temporary path copies to 64KiB per batch, avoiding large untracked memory spikes on long shared prefixes by @madolson (#5179)

### Bug Fixes
* Reject module write commands while the server is paused for writes, preventing a crash from module timer callbacks during `CLIENT PAUSE WRITE` or `CLUSTER FAILOVER` by @smkher (#3645)
* Fix event loop busy-spinning on virtual machines by not using raw TSC for the monotonic clock when the kernel clocksource is not tsc by @quanyeyang (#4707)
* Fix a crash in `ValkeyModule_HashHasStringRef` on a missing or expired field and correct wrong return values in the hash stringRef module APIs by @ShubhamTaple (#4504)
* Fix a server abort on a RESTORE payload declaring a string length that overflows the allocation size; such payloads are now rejected as bad data by @enjoy-binbin (#4733)
* Fix ZINTER/ZINTERSTORE returning input-order-dependent scores when a weighted term is 0*inf; a NaN weighted score now counts as 0, matching ZUNION by @leomurillo (#4997)
* Fix crashes, lookup hangs, and duplicate set members when keys or elements reach 2 GiB, caused by storing string lengths in a 32-bit integer by @madolson (#5133)
* Fix module global defrag resuming on the wrong module or with a stale cursor when `MODULE UNLOAD` runs between defrag cycles by @madolson (#5154)
* Propagate `PFADD` elements applied before a corrupted-HLL INVALIDOBJ error so replicas and the AOF stay consistent with the primary by @madolson (#5128)
* Fix a server crash in `SCRIPT DEBUG SYNC` mode when a debugger command arrives split across more than one read by @madolson (#5127)
* Fix a server panic when a Lua script returns or raises an error table whose metatable has an `__index` metamethod that raises an error by @madolson (#5118)
* Fix forkless BGSAVE producing a corrupt snapshot when `SWAPDB` runs without being replicated, such as from a script with replication disabled by @madolson (#5116)
* Let `FLUSHALL` and `SHUTDOWN` cancel a forkless save that is finalizing its file, so a stale snapshot can no longer overwrite the newer dump.rdb by @madolson (#5121)
* Fix a server crash when a module never sets a postponed reply length; the leftover placeholder is now filled with an empty array by @madolson (#5159)
* Fix a memory leak when `server.register_function` named arguments are repeated in a different letter case by @madolson (#5120)
* Preserve expired but not yet reaped hash fields across listpack-to-hashtable conversion so their deletion is properly reaped and propagated by @frostzt (#4704)
* Fix a double-decremented item count when background iteration is terminated with a SWAPDB or FLUSHDB event queued by @JimB123 (#4750)
* Fix `GEOSEARCH` returning empty results for exact zero-distance matches on builds where floating-point contraction breaks the latitude distance calculation by @Baraa-Hasheesh (#4777)
* Reject inline commands containing a raw NUL byte with a protocol error instead of leaving the connection stalled by @cjx-zar (#4759)
* Fix a memory leak on normal shutdown caused by I/O worker threads not being terminated and cleaned up by @roshkhatri (#4710)
* `XACKDEL` with `KEEPREF` now replies 1 instead of -1 when acknowledging an entry whose stream message was already deleted, matching the ACKED and DELREF modes by @adityamukesh (#4843)
* Fix listpack encoding incompatibility that caused RDB load and replication failures for entries of certain lengths between 9.0 and 9.1.x by @jjuleslasarte (#4819)
* Reject relative expire times in `SET`/`GETEX`, `RESTORE`, and `ValkeyModule_SetExpire` that overflow when added to the current time, preventing server aborts from negative expires by @madolson (#4880)
* `ACL DIGEST` now includes role definitions, so editing a role's rules changes the reported fingerprint by @melancholictheory (#4694)
* Fix a server crash when loading an ACL file containing a selector with an unmatched parenthesis by @magic-peach (#4214)
* Fix a segfault on Alpine/musl when Lua is built as a module, caused by a symbol clash on an internal clock function by @mohammedgqudah (#4270)
* Fix lex range seeks, NaN score bound handling, and a memory leak in B+tree sorted sets, and resolve `ZRANGEBYLEX` LIMIT offsets in logarithmic time by @xiaocj (#4644)
* Fix expired hash fields left untracked after listpack-to-hashtable conversion, which could crash the server on a later write and leave fields that are never reaped by @beyondwin (#4894)
* Restore acceptance of hexadecimal float sorted set scores (such as `0x10`), keeping replication and AOF replay compatible with Valkey 9.0 by @quanyeyang (#4875)
* Sorted set range commands with a negative `LIMIT` offset now return an empty result instead of a spurious element on btree-encoded keys by @xiaocj (#4637)
* Fix `HSETEX` and `HGETEX` failing to parse their arguments when the key is named `fields` by @sebxt (#4945)
* Fix a crash when active defrag's deferred keys outlive a keyspace replacement such as FLUSHDB/FLUSHALL ASYNC, SWAPDB, or a replica's pre-sync flush by @taham0 (#4968)
* Fix `LSET` on 64-bit builds silently modifying the wrong element for out-of-range indexes instead of returning an index out of range error by @charsyam (#4823)
* Fix a heap buffer overflow in cluster Pub/Sub message construction; oversized PUBLISH and SPUBLISH payloads are now rejected with an error in cluster mode by @roshkhatri (#5030)
* Lex range commands on btree-encoded sorted sets with mixed scores now match listpack results, preventing primary/replica divergence via ZREMRANGEBYLEX and ZRANGESTORE by @pirate329 (#4954)
* Fix a memory leak when `GEOSEARCH` or `GEOSEARCHSTORE` is given repeated `BYPOLYGON` options by @charsyam (#4995)
* `DEBUG RELOAD` and `DEBUG LOADAOF` now return a LOADING error while the dataset is loading, avoiding a possible panic by @enjoy-binbin (#4877)
* Fix a memory leak in `ValkeyModule_GetCommandKeysWithFlags` when introspecting commands with large key lists by @christopherlim98 (#5046)
* `MEMORY USAGE` now counts hash fields that have expired but not yet been reaped, fixing under-reported sizes by @sushilpaneru1 (#5092)
* Fix a crash in `ValkeyModule_Call` when script-mode validation fails and error replies were not requested by @dvkashapov (#5091)
* High-priority socket events are no longer drained when the event loop caller did not request file event processing by @enjoy-binbin (#5098)
* Fix a crash when a replication role change command such as `REPLICAOF` or `CLUSTER REPLICATE` arrives over a replication link by @madolson (#5187)
* `FUNCTION RESTORE` now applies the same library load timeout as `FUNCTION LOAD`, so a never-returning library can no longer block the server forever by @madolson (#5181)
* Fix a buffer overflow in valkey-benchmark when `--num-functions` is large enough to overflow the generated script buffer by @madolson (#5175)
* Fix a valkey-check-rdb crash with `--stats` on RDB files whose highest selected database contains no keys by @madolson (#5177)
* Fix a crash on the importing primary when an atomic slot migration fails while its writes are paused by @madolson (#5182)
* Fix `GEOSEARCH BYPOLYGON` missing matching members when the polygon's vertex centroid falls outside the valid latitude range by @madolson (#5174)
* Fix a primary abort when `CLUSTER SETSLOT` runs inside MULTI or a script on a primary with online replicas by @madolson (#5141)
* Fix a memory leak when deleting or replacing Lua functions with long names or descriptions by @madolson (#5109)
* A refused oversized `XADD` no longer creates an empty stream key that replicas and the AOF never receive by @madolson (#5178)
* Prevent a replica crash when the primary wrongly replies +CONTINUE to a full resync request; the replica now drops the link and retries by @madolson (#5126)
* FUNCTION LOAD no longer aborts the server when a library calls `server.log()` at its top level, including when loading from RDB or AOF by @madolson (#5114)
* RESET on a slot migration connection now returns an error instead of crashing the server with an assertion failure by @madolson (#5140)
* DEBUG SLOTMIGRATION with missing arguments now returns an error instead of crashing the server by @madolson (#5147)
* KEYS on a flushed database no longer leaks a rehashing pause that permanently stops rehashing and can eventually crash the server by @madolson (#5166)
* Automatic RDB snapshots and AOF rewrites are no longer postponed while a forked SCRIPT DEBUG session is open by @madolson (#5153)
* Fix an integer overflow in quicklist node merging that could crash the server on lists loaded with nodes over 4GiB via RESTORE or replication by @madolson (#5163)
* Fix a stack buffer overflow when replying with hundreds of empty strings (e.g. MGET) while reply copy avoidance is active by @madolson (#5151)
* CLUSTER SLOT-STATS ORDERBY no longer replies with uninitialized slot entries when a node's primary is itself a replica that claims slots by @madolson (#5131)
* Fix a race with TLS and io-threads where an IO thread still writing to a client could modify the main thread's event loop by @madolson (#5156)
* Fix a replica crash when a script exceeding busy-reply-threshold ends during CLIENT PAUSE WRITE with a pending replicated write by @madolson (#5150)
* In cluster mode, one cross-slot command in a script no longer makes every later script and function call fail until restart by @madolson (#5191)
* Fix a use-after-free crash when a forkless save is running while a swapdb-mode full sync swaps in the primary's keyspace on a replica by @nitaicaro (#5082)
* Fix a replica assertion crash when the primary writes a key still in use by a forkless (consistent) save by @harrylin98 (#5206)
* Fix a dangling pointer when a key is deleted during a forkless save, which could crash or silently corrupt the iteration by @JimB123 (#4996)
* Clear the script debugger input buffer after a "max client buffer reached" error so later debugger commands in the same session do not keep failing by @madolson (#5129)

### Command and API Updates
* Correct command metadata to describe the `ZINCRBY` increment and `ZINTER`/`ZINTERSTORE`/`ZUNION`/`ZUNIONSTORE` weights as doubles instead of integers by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5210)
* Correct command metadata so the `numfields` count argument of hash field commands is no longer associated with a key specification by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5211)
* Correct expiry command metadata to show that `XX` can be combined with `GT` or `LT`, rather than all four conditions being mutually exclusive by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5213)
* Mark the `RESTORE` and `RESTORE-ASKING` `IDLETIME` and `FREQ` options as mutually exclusive in command metadata by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5212)
* Correct the `HEXPIRE`, `HPEXPIRE`, `HEXPIREAT`, and `HPEXPIREAT` command summaries to say they set expiration on hash fields, not the hash object by @poiuj (#4783)
* Add `LBOUND`, `UBOUND`, `SATURATE`, `ENX`, and `PERSIST` options to `INCREX` for bounded increments and conditional expiration control by @murphyjacob4 (#4679)
* Correct `SENTINEL SIMULATE-FAILURE` metadata so `COMMAND DOCS` shows the required mode argument and its tokens by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5208)
* Rename the Path Hash command `PHEXISTS` to `PHPATHEXISTS` to clarify that it checks a path rather than a hash field by @yangbodong22011 (#5069)
* Add `PHPATHSCAN` for ordered incremental path iteration and change `PHSCAN` to iterate fields and values at an exact path by @yangbodong22011 (#5066)
* Remove `PHLONGEST` in favor of `PHPREFIXES`, which now returns matches longest-first with paging and an `EXCLUDESELF` option by @yangbodong22011 (#5070)
* Replace `PHCARD` with `PHPATHCOUNT`, which can also count only the paths under a given prefix by @yangbodong22011 (#5071)
* Replace `PHDELPREFIX` with `PHPATHDEL key path [WITHSUBPATHS]`, which deletes an exact path or its whole subtree and returns the number of deleted paths by @yangbodong22011 (#5067)
* Mark the absolute timestamp arguments of `HEXPIREAT` and `HPEXPIREAT` as `unix-time` in `COMMAND DOCS`, matching `EXPIREAT` and `PEXPIREAT` by @rainsupreme (#5245)
* Correct `ZADD` and `LCS` metadata so `COMMAND DOCS` and valkey-cli hints no longer present `NX` with `GT`/`LT` or `LEN` with `IDX` as valid combinations by @rainsupreme (#5244)

### Cluster and Replication
* Decouple `rdbcompression` (on-disk RDB format) from `repl-compression` (replication wire format) so setting one no longer affects the other during a full sync by @zuiderkwast (#4749)
* Avoid rapid failover election restarts by fast-failing only on NACK reasons that a new election epoch can actually fix by @enjoy-binbin (#4700)
* Prevent a failover auth NACK for an old election from being counted against the current election by echoing the rejected request epoch by @xdk-amz (#4654)
* Keep a replica's connection to its primary on the main thread so replication flow control works when I/O threads are enabled by @chky1386 (#4765)
* `HDEL`, `HGETDEL`, `HPERSIST`, and `HEXPIRE` no longer propagate fields they treat as expired, preventing replica and AOF-reload divergence by @xdk-amz (#4772)
* `COPY` of a hash now includes expired-but-unreaped fields so their deletion is propagated and replicas stay in sync by @pirate329 (#4939)
* Fix atomic slot migration not replicating evictions on the import target, which let replicas grow far past `maxmemory` by @shanezx-sc (#4920)
* Fix cluster config saving to avoid publishing truncated `nodes.conf` files, losing the startup lock after the first save, and failing every save on SMB filesystems such as Azure Files; the lock now lives on a separate `nodes.conf.lock` file by @KewangZhili (#4489)
* Fix failover election fast-fail double-counting a voter that rejected the request and was later marked FAIL, which could abandon a winnable election by @xdk-amz (#4655)
* Fix atomic slot migration with `cluster-databases` > 1 applying writes made during the snapshot to the wrong database on the target by @pirate329 (#4952)
* Ignore new nodes gossiped by a sender still in handshake so a forged MEET packet cannot fill the cluster node table by @madolson (#5145)
* Ignore invalid ping extension values from cluster peers that would corrupt nodes.conf and prevent the node from restarting by @madolson (#5137)
* Bound the bytes the cluster bus reads per event so a peer with a constant read backlog cannot starve clients, cron and heartbeats by @madolson (#5161)
* Fix incorrect missing-key handling of replicated MULTI/EXEC transactions during a forkless full sync by @JimB123 (#5205)

### Configuration
* CONFIG REWRITE now quotes the replicaof host, so hosts with spaces or newlines no longer corrupt the config file by @madolson (#5176)
* Rename the `bgsave-default-method` config to `forkless-policy` with values `require-fork` and `prefer-forkless` by @madolson (#5261)

### Module API Changes
* `ValkeyModule_ScanKey` and `ValkeyModule_ScanKeyRawBorrowed` no longer expose expired-but-unreaped fields of listpack-encoded hashes to modules by @madolson (#4885)
* Fix module zset range iteration returning duplicate or phantom elements when changing direction on B+tree encoded sorted sets by @xiaocj (#4645)
* Allow modules to block RESP3 clients that are subscribed to Pub/Sub channels instead of failing `ValkeyModule_BlockClient` with ENOTSUP by @quanyeyang (#4863)
* Make `ValkeyModule_CallArgv` public, letting modules invoke commands with lower overhead through reply callbacks by @dvkashapov (#3911)

### Observability and Logging
* Attribute LZ4 replication compression context memory to client memory usage so it appears under client memory accounting by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4702)
* Redact error text in server logs when `hide-user-data-from-log` is enabled, so command arguments no longer leak into logs by @zackcam (#4815)
* Redact credentials of rejected `HELLO`, `AUTH` and `MIGRATE` commands so passwords no longer leak to MONITOR and the commandlog by @madolson (#5180)
* Replace line breaks in Lua `server.log()` messages with spaces so scripts cannot forge standalone server log records by @madolson (#5185)

### CLI and Tools
* valkey-check-aof now recognizes RDB base files with the `VALKEY` signature instead of misreporting a valid multipart AOF as invalid by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4739)
* Increase the `valkey-benchmark` maximum latency histogram value from 3 to 60 seconds so slow requests are reported accurately by @gabiganam (#3157)
* Fix valkey-benchmark spinning on would-block writes, which could starve reply processing and the `--duration` timer by @thweetkomputer (#4567)
* Support bracketed IPv6 addresses such as `[::1]:7000` in `valkey-cli --cluster` commands by @chenshi5012 (#4800)
* Fix an unbalanced `]` in valkey-cli command hints for commands with repeated optional arguments such as BITFIELD_RO by @ShubhamTaple (#3974)
* valkey-cli no longer prints the command line password warning when the password comes only from `VALKEYCLI_AUTH` or `REDISCLI_AUTH` by @madolson (#4886)
* valkey-cli now rejects a zero or negative `--hotkeys-count` instead of attempting a huge allocation and aborting by @madolson (#5173)
* valkey-cli now skips RESP3 attributes instead of exiting with an unknown reply type error by @madolson (#5186)
* valkey-check-rdb now prints usage when `--output` is given without a file name instead of crashing by @madolson (#5135)
* valkey-benchmark no longer aborts loading a CSV dataset whose last field in a row is a lone quote; the quote is kept literally by @madolson (#5168)

### Build and Tooling
* Link macOS example and test modules through the compiler driver so builds no longer fail on newer SDKs' libSystem stubs by @avifenesh (#4927)
* Rebuild the Lua scripting module during incremental builds when its sources change, so edits are no longer silently left out of `valkey-server` by @madolson (#5242)

### Behavior Changes
* `ZRANGEBYSCORE`, `ZREVRANGEBYSCORE`, `ZCOUNT`, and `ZRANGESTORE` now reject a bare `(` or an empty string as a score bound instead of silently treating it as 0 by @AlisinaDevelo (#4054)
* Path Hash deletion commands now remove the key when the last path is deleted, following the Hash key lifecycle and emitting a generic del event by @yangbodong22011 (#5068)

Valkey 9.2.0-rc1  -  Released Wed 16 September 2026
---------------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency LOW: This is the first release candidate of Valkey 9.2.0.

### Behavior Changes
* Active expiration of keys and hash fields now increments the dirty counter, so save points (and thus BGSAVE) may trigger more often by @enjoy-binbin (#3118)

### New Features and Enhanced Behavior
* Add ACL DIGEST command that returns a fingerprint of the ACL rules currently in effect, useful to verify what ACL LOAD applied by @melancholictheory (#4446)
* Add forkless RDB snapshots, opt-in via the new `forkless-infrastructure-enabled` and `bgsave-default-method` configs, with new INFO persistence fields reporting the save method and progress by @JimB123 (#4460)
* Add the `XACKDEL` and `XDELEX` stream commands with `KEEPREF`, `DELREF` and `ACKED` modes to acknowledge and delete messages once consumer groups no longer need them by @nickiaq (#4629)
* Support a secondary server certificate via `tls-alt-cert-file`, `tls-alt-key-file` and `tls-alt-key-file-pass`, e.g. a post-quantum certificate alongside RSA, with matching INFO TLS fields by @pkhartsk (#3717)
* Add ACL roles: named, reusable sets of ACL selectors managed with `ACL SETROLE`/`DELROLE`/`GETROLE`/`ROLES` and assigned to users with `role:<name>`, in commands, the ACL file and valkey.conf by @yang-z-o (#3967)
* Add a `maxmemory-scripts` config to limit memory used by cached `EVAL` scripts, and mark `SCRIPT LOAD` as DENYOOM so it respects the global maxmemory limit by @enjoy-binbin (#866)
* Add Path Hash, a new radix-tree-backed data type with `PH*` commands for exact lookup, longest-prefix matching, and prefix traversal over binary-safe paths by @yangbodong22011 (#4506)
* Support whole-stream LZ4 compression of RDB files via the new `rdbcompression lz4` option; the default per-string LZF behavior is unchanged by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#3531)
* Add server-side hot key detection with new `HOTKEYS GET`/`RESET` commands, enabled by setting `hotkeys-top-k` by @alon-arenberg (#3708)
* Add optional replication throttling (`repl-throttling-enabled`) that slows client writes when a replica falls behind, avoiding disconnects and full syncs by @harrylin98 (#4356)
* Prioritize system-critical events (cluster heartbeats, replication, slot migration) over heavy client traffic, tunable via the new `priority-preemptive-poll-interval-us` config by @satheeshaGowda (#4076)
* Reserve connection slots for administrative clients: connections from the CIDR ranges listed in the new `priority-subnets` config are tagged as prioritized, `maxclients-reserved` caps normal clients at `maxclients` minus that many slots, and `INFO clients` reports `connected_priority_clients` by @satheeshaGowda (#4005)
* Add `INCREX` command to atomically increment a key by an integer or float while setting its expiration, with `NX`/`XX` conditions by @GavinDmello (#3253)

### Performance and Efficiency Improvements
* Speed up radix tree lookups and inserts by using SIMD-optimized memchr() for child-edge search by @charsyam (#3472)
* Improve replica processing speed by parsing multiple commands from the replication stream at once by @enjoy-binbin (#3597)
* Reduce memory usage by sharing pubsub pattern and WATCH key objects across clients subscribing to or watching the same name by @enjoy-binbin (#4072)
* Large sorted sets are now backed by a B+ tree instead of a skiplist; OBJECT ENCODING reports `btree` instead of `skiplist` by @ranshid (#4359)
* Save the cluster config file from a background thread when `cluster-config-save-behavior` is best-effort, avoiding main-thread latency spikes from slow disk I/O by @enjoy-binbin (#2555)
* Speed up `HMGET`, `SMISMEMBER` and `ZMSCORE` on large hashtable-encoded keys with batched lookups that overlap memory accesses by @chzhoo (#4017)
* Extend memory prefetching to hash, set and sorted set member lookups when io-threads are enabled, improving performance for 30 field/member commands on large keys by @roshkhatri (#3940)
* `MEMORY PURGE` now also releases free pages from the glibc main arena back to the OS, reclaiming memory held by libc-internal allocations by @webbsssss (#3640)
* Speed up command propagation to replicas by batching each command's RESP frame into a single replication buffer write by @hpatro (#4044)
* Reduce lseek system calls during disk-based replication by seeking only when a write blocks or is partial by @enjoy-binbin (#4053)
* Reduce event-loop overhead by refreshing cached daylight-saving info once per second instead of on every wakeup by @hpatro (#4086)
* Speed up keyspace event notifications by skipping work when there are no subscribers and avoiding unnecessary allocations by @enjoy-binbin (#4285)
* Speed up exact `XTRIM MAXLEN = 0` by about 2.5x by clearing the whole stream in one step instead of removing entries individually by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4161)
* Cluster bus reads, writes, and inbound TLS accepts can now run on the shared I/O thread pool, with new `CLUSTER INFO` offload statistics by @hpatro (#3438)
* Small hashes with field expiration now use the memory-efficient listpack encoding instead of always converting to a hashtable by @frostzt (#3212)
* Reduce per-command overhead by skipping post-command bookkeeping when no propagation, module, or invalidation work is pending by @ahmetalicc (#4257)

### Bug Fixes
* MODULE LOAD is now rejected during async replication loading and atomic slot migration to avoid unexpected module behavior by @KIvanow (#3039)
* Reject CLUSTER ADDSLOTS/DELSLOTS/ADDSLOTSRANGE/DELSLOTSRANGE/FLUSHSLOTS on replicas, preventing an assertion failure on a later CLUSTER REPLICATE by @enjoy-binbin (#4020)
* Fix a crash when processing a heartbeat from a cluster node whose role is locally unknown, such as after loading an incomplete nodes.conf by @enjoy-binbin (#4091)
* Fix wrong results or debug-build assertions in cluster mode when the server inspects keys outside the executing command's slot, such as WATCHed keys checked during EXEC by @nitaicaro (#4380)
* Fix stream commands that mutate consumer-group or PEL state (`XGROUP`, `XSETID`, `XREADGROUP`, `XACK`, `XCLAIM`, `XAUTOCLAIM`) not triggering `WATCH` and client-side tracking invalidation by @Tarte12 (#3459)
* Fix a server crash on FUNCTION DELETE or FUNCTION LOAD REPLACE after loading a library with function names differing only in case by @madolson (#3925)
* Client-side tracking no longer records routing-only tokens such as the CLUSTERSCAN cursor as tracked keys by @nmvk (#3699)
* Reject malformed slot entries in the cluster config file as a corrupt config instead of asserting or invoking undefined behavior by @enjoy-binbin (#4100)
* Fix a TLS busy loop that consumed 100% CPU when a connection's read or write handler was removed while OpenSSL was waiting for the opposite event by @yairgott (#3510)
* Client eviction no longer disconnects extra clients when a large client's close is deferred but its memory is already scheduled to be freed by @dhruv2x (#4152)
* Fix a crash caused by a NULL pointer dereference when all timer events in an event loop are pending deletion by @royenheart (#4351)
* Rework iteration over clients blocked on ready keys to simplify and harden an earlier use-after-free fix by @enjoy-binbin (#4472)
* Fix a race in RDB string compression that could produce corrupt, unloadable RDB files when compression runs concurrently, without increasing copy-on-write by @dubey02 (#4539)
* Fix dropped field TTLs and a possible crash when loading a hash with field expiration converts it to a hashtable mid-load (e.g. via RESTORE) by @madolson (#4669)
* Reject a repeated `CLUSTER SYNCSLOTS ESTABLISH` on the same connection, which could lead to a use-after-free crash on disconnect by @Pyolar (#4670)
* Fix wrong `ZCOUNT` results and incorrect `ZREMRANGEBYSCORE` deletions when members sharing a boundary score span multiple btree leaves by @rainsupreme (#4554)
* Fix `SORT` key extraction so a `STORE` destination named like an option can no longer bypass ACL checks and write to an unauthorized key by @madolson (#4665)

### Command and API Updates
* `MOVE` accepts a new optional `REPLACE` argument to overwrite an existing key in the destination database by @bandalgomsu (#2993)
* WAIT and WAITAOF now reject numreplicas values that are negative or exceed INT_MAX, fixing an integer overflow that broke blocking by @enjoy-binbin (#3407)
* Add CONFIG INFO subcommand returning config metadata such as type, flags, valid enum values and numeric ranges by @nitaicaro (#3050)
* Add the `IFNE` option to `SET` to set a key only when its current value differs from the given comparison value by @arshidkv12 (#3105)
* Add `IFEQ`, `IFNE`, `NX` and `XX` conditions to `EXEC`, enabling optimistic locking for multi-key transactions without `WATCH` by @bandalgomsu (#4019)
* Add an optional `XX` flag to `SISMEMBER` that returns -1 when the key does not exist, distinguishing a missing key from a missing member by @li-benson (#2972)
* Handle NOT_KEY key-specs more defensively so COMMAND GETKEYS and ACL key checks consistently treat routing-only tokens as non-keys by @enjoy-binbin (#3675)
* Fix DEBUG HELP to show the correct DELAY-RDB-CLIENT-FREE-SECONDS name and document the SET-DISABLE-DENY-SCRIPTS subcommand by @xiejing-dev (#4099)
* Add XX option to the ZRANGE family of commands to distinguish a non-existent key (nil) from an empty result by @youngmore1024 (#2978)
* Fix the reply schemas of the ZRANGE family of commands to allow the null reply returned with the XX option by @murphyjacob4 (#4275)
* Fix the `XPENDING` reply schema to describe the summary reply returned when a consumer group has no pending messages by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4653)

### Cluster and Replication
* Cluster replicas now redirect keyless commands like SCAN and FLUSHDB to the primary for clients with CAPA REDIRECT that have not sent READONLY by @yanamolo (#3505)
* Changing cluster-require-full-coverage via CONFIG SET now updates the cluster state immediately instead of waiting for the next cron cycle by @enjoy-binbin (#3676)
* Fix CLUSTER BUMPEPOCH getting stuck when a dead node holds an equal or abnormally high config epoch; a single bump now overtakes it by @enjoy-binbin (#4092)
* Replicas now retry PSYNC when the primary replies -BUSY instead of downgrading to legacy SYNC, which broke WAIT, PSYNC and FAILOVER by @enjoy-binbin (#4140)
* SYNC/PSYNC from a replica with a down primary link now consistently returns -NOMASTERLINK, avoiding an unnecessary full sync fallback by @enjoy-binbin (#4148)
* Add cluster-replica-priority config so operators can rank which replicas are preferred during automatic cluster failover by @enjoy-binbin (#2204)
* Speed up recovery from split-vote failover elections with a new FAILOVER_AUTH_NACK message that lets a replica detect an unwinnable election and immediately retry with a higher epoch by @enjoy-binbin (#3833)
* Add optional per-target `AUTH username password` to `CLUSTER MIGRATESLOTS`, with credentials redacted from the slow log and MONITOR by @nemtsv (#3538)
* Compress the full-sync RDB payload with LZ4 when `rdbcompression lz4` is set and every attaching replica advertises support, reducing sync bandwidth with safe fallback to plaintext by @roshkhatri (#4075)
* Add an `if-empty` value to `cluster-replica-no-failover` so a replica that has never received data from its primary refuses automatic failover, preventing silent data loss by @enjoy-binbin (#4425)
* Add optional LZ4 streaming compression for steady-state replication via the new `repl-compression` config, negotiated per replica so older or opted-out replicas keep receiving plaintext by @roshkhatri (#3853)
* Fix `CLUSTERSCAN` fingerprints to derive from the hash-seed config so cursors survive failover between nodes sharing a seed by @enjoy-binbin (#3679)
* Replicas trigger a failover check immediately when cluster-replica-no-failover is disabled at runtime, instead of waiting for the next cron tick by @enjoy-binbin (#3827)
* Validate node IDs and shard IDs received in cluster messages before applying them, dropping the link on invalid data to protect cluster state by @enjoy-binbin (#4065)
* Drop the cluster link when a gossip section contains invalid node IDs, instead of keeping the connection to a corrupted sender alive by @enjoy-binbin (#4077)
* Persist nodes.conf promptly when a node's address is updated through the gossip section by @enjoy-binbin (#4089)
* Reject malformed node IDs in the open-slots RDB aux field instead of creating an illegal cluster node by @enjoy-binbin (#4098)
* Strip the redundant LIMIT option when rewriting XADD/XTRIM for propagation, so the rewritten command is valid for tools that replay it by @cjx-zar (#4063)
* Persist non-default cluster-replica-priority to nodes.conf so it survives restarts instead of waiting for the next gossip round by @enjoy-binbin (#4454)
* Clear a stale primary-failure gossip flag on replicas so later failovers don't incorrectly skip the election delay by @charsyam (#4533)
* Fix a node staying stuck in PFAIL when its PING is lost while the peer's own traffic keeps the cluster link alive by @enjoy-binbin (#4171)
* `CLUSTER SYNCSLOTS FINISH` now rejects clients outside the slot migration stream, preventing misuse of the import state machine by @enjoy-binbin (#4330)

### Configuration
* `commandlog-request-larger-than` and `commandlog-reply-larger-than` now accept memory units such as 10mb by @enjoy-binbin (#2648)
* `cluster-announce-ip` now must be a valid IP address or hostname, rejecting values like `ip:port` that broke cluster bus addressing by @AlisinaDevelo (#4055)
* Reject an empty `tls-ca-cert-dir` at startup and `CONFIG SET` time instead of silently accepting it and failing every client handshake later by @yang-z-o (#3522)
* Document the database-level ACL rules (`db=`, `alldbs`, `resetdbs`) in valkey.conf and clarify the `reset` rule description by @enjoy-binbin (#3808)
* CONFIG REWRITE now preserves module load order, so modules with dependencies load correctly after a restart by @Taeknology (#3769)
* Document in valkey.conf that unixsocketgroup requires the chown syscall to be allowed under syscall-filtering sandboxes by @moko-poi (#3730)

### Module API Changes
* Add `ValkeyModule_ScanKeyRawBorrowed` to scan hash, set and sorted set keys without allocating a string per element by @KarthikSubbarao (#4403)
* Fix loading of legacy Redis modules that export `RedisModule_OnLoad` via a linker version script by @roshkhatri (#3374)
* Module global defrag callbacks now receive a time limit and a resumable cursor, making `ValkeyModule_RegisterDefragFunc` usable for large module data by @Aksha1812 (#4487)
* Add `ValkeyModule_IncrExternalMemory`/`DecrExternalMemory` so modules can report memory allocated outside the server allocator toward `used_memory` and `maxmemory` by @bandalgomsu (#4128)
* Correct `ValkeyModule_FreeModuleUser`, `ValkeyModule_ACLAddLogEntry` and `ValkeyModule_ACLAddLogEntryByUserName` declarations to return int as implemented, fixing undefined behavior on targets with strict call signature checks by @rainsupreme (#4676)

### Observability and Logging
* Client memory usage now includes watched key and pubsub channel/pattern names, making it visible in CLIENT INFO tot-mem and counted for maxmemory-clients by @enjoy-binbin (#3362)
* CONFIG RESETSTAT now also resets the IO-thread prefetch and ACL access-denied statistics by @enjoy-binbin (#2891)
* Latency report now recommends 'madvise' for disabling Transparent Huge Pages, consistent with the startup check by @enjoy-binbin (#3947)
* Log when a cluster primary ignores an MFSTART manual failover message from an unknown node or a non-replica, helping diagnose failover timeouts by @enjoy-binbin (#4058)
* Log a warning when a TLS certificate has an invalid notBefore or notAfter field on OpenSSL 4.0 builds by @pkhartsk (#4064)
* Gossip corruption warnings now log the actual entry with the invalid node ID instead of the first gossip entry by @enjoy-binbin (#4101)
* Produce crash stack traces on musl-based systems like Alpine Linux via a libbacktrace fallback by @hanxizh9910 (#3581)
* Always log the "possibly failing" notice when a node enters PFAIL, including on voting primaries by @enjoy-binbin (#4186)
* `EXEC` transactions are now recorded in the slowlog and commandlog when their total execution time crosses the threshold by @michellee-10 (#4267)
* Add `last_successful_sync_duration_ms` to `INFO replication`, reporting how long the replica's last full sync took by @satheeshaGowda (#4197)
* Fix signal mask parsing on 32-bit systems so the crash handler can collect thread stack traces by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#4415)
* Add `total_cluster_links_established_inbound`/`outbound` counters to `CLUSTER INFO` to help detect cluster link flapping by @enjoy-binbin (#4169)
* RDMA connection and resource setup failures are now logged with detailed system error information by @quanyeyang (#4586)
* Include the LRU list's duplicated script SHA copies in EVAL script memory reporting (`used_memory_scripts_eval`) by @enjoy-binbin (#4587)
* Log the module version alongside the module name when a module is loaded, so the loaded version is visible in the log by @enjoy-binbin (#4566)
* Detect changes to the alternate TLS key file (`tls-alt-key-file`) so certificate auto-reload picks them up by @pkhartsk (#4663)
* Report `tls_server_cert_serial` and expiry INFO fields for the certificate actually loaded from `tls-cert-file` instead of whichever one OpenSSL slots first by @madolson (#4664)

### CLI and Tools
* valkey-cli reads the `VALKEYCLI_HOST` and `VALKEYCLI_PORT` environment variables to set the default host and port by @Dietr1ch (#3402)
* valkey-benchmark can load CSV/TSV datasets and inject their fields into commands via `__field:name__` placeholders by @VoletiRam (#2823)
* valkey-cli supports the VALKEYCLI_USER environment variable as an alternative to the --user option by @jdheyburn (#4126)
* `valkey-cli --rdb` now exits with an error instead of reporting success when trimming the RDB EOF marker fails, avoiding a silently corrupt file by @gluxier (#3945)
* Fix valkey-benchmark crash (out-of-bounds read) when a repeat count is given with no command following it by @lightsigma96 (#4142)
* valkey-benchmark -r now accepts keyspace sizes above INT_MAX (up to 999,999,999,999) with proper input validation by @michellee-10 (#4252)
* valkey-benchmark now rejects a repeat count with no command after it with a clear error instead of hanging forever sending zero requests by @dhruv2x (#4215)
* valkey-benchmark multi-threaded mode scales further by removing cross-thread contention in key generation, latency recording, and counters by @rainsupreme (#4332)

### Build and Tooling
* Add REUSE-compliant machine-readable licensing with per-file license clarity, enabling SPDX SBOM generation and correct license detection by @zuiderkwast (#3968)
* Fix clean or highly parallel builds failing with a missing release.h for valkey-cli, valkey-benchmark, and unit tests by @poiuj (#3683)
* Use PRIVATE link dependencies in CMake so Valkey's CMake files can be safely integrated into other projects by @eifrah-aws (#3658)
* Pass `CPPFLAGS` to bundled dependencies and the src Makefile so packaging hardening flags apply to the whole build by @Vonng (#4318)
